06_build/*
!06_build/contracts.md

*.kicad_pcb-bak
*.kicad_sch-bak
*-backups/
_autosave-*
fp-info-cache

__pycache__/
*.kicad_prl

# tscircuit build cache + intermediate export (mirrors usb-hub-3s-v3; commit build/ kicad/ verification/ only)
03_tscircuit/.tscircuit/
03_tscircuit/dist/

# failed routing-attempt artifacts
*.failed
# transient stitch scratch: route_and_stitch carries counters across its SWIG
# re-exec barrier in <board>.kicad_pcb.stitch_state.json and deletes it on a
# clean finish. A tracked copy only ever means a run was killed mid-stitch
# (one was, at pass 5/22, and it got committed along with a .failed board).
*.stitch_state.json
# kicad-cli DROPPING. Opening `<board>.kicad_pcb` with kicad-cli writes a
# throwaway project beside it named `<board>.kicad_pcb.kicad_pro` (note: the
# .kicad_pcb stays IN the name — it is not the board's real .kicad_pro). It is
# regenerated by every DRC/gerber run, and the 07_releases seal procedure makes
# sweeping it the FINAL pre-seal check because it bit two boards on 2026-07-23.
# A rule is better than a sweep: an ignored dropping cannot dirty a seal.
# It is ALSO load-bearing for this project specifically — rebuild_all.sh runs
# generate_rules in a shadow root precisely because generate_rules_generic
# aborts when 04_kicad holds more than one .kicad_pro, and this dropping is a
# second one.
*.kicad_pcb.kicad_pro
